iscovering childbase.com is a broken/misconfigured domain (SSL certificate mismatch, and even with -k a SiteGround default-vhost stub -- the real domain is childbasepartnership.com, found via a DuckDuckGo web search) -- fetched its actual childcare-services Terms and Conditions, arguably an even better fit for this occupation than a generic corporate ToU. G8 Education Limited (ASX-listed Australian childcare operator, GLEIF relationship data confirms no parent via an explicit reporting-exception) succeeded, but no general consumer Website Terms of Use was discoverable on its corporate site after multiple guessed paths and an XML-sitemap check -- its Privacy Policy was used as the closest real, substantive published legal document instead, honestly recorded as :privacy-policy not :terms-of-service (same substitution precedent as Visa in the sibling universe-progress.edn). People and Baby (French crèche/nursery group, GLEIF relationship data confirms no parent via reporting-exception) was GLEIF-verified but failed ToS fetch: HTTP 403 via curl on 3 URL attempts against the correct domain (found via its French Wikipedia infobox, since www.people-and-baby.fr and the visually-similar peopleandbaby.com are wrong/parked domains), and a WebFetch retry on the same URL returned only a paraphrased summary for a related-but-distinct legal entity ('People and Baby Développement', a different SIREN than the GLEIF-registered 'People and Baby' entity) rather than confirmed verbatim text for the exact GLEIF entity -- recorded as a clean :tos-fetch-failed rather than accepting an unverified paraphrase. Three additional candidates were researched and excluded before any ToS fetch attempt, same discipline as the original KinderCare/Learning Care Group exclusions: Busy Bees Group and Kids R Kids International both have no GLEIF record under that name (NO RECORDS from the GLEIF API for either); Cognita Schools / Cognita Limited has no direct GLEIF record either, but a related entity 'Cognita Holdings Limited' does exist -- its GLEIF relationship data shows it has both a direct-parent ('Lernen Bidco Limited') and an ultimate-parent ('Lernen Topco Limited'), i.e. it is itself a subsidiary of an opaque private-equity holding-vehicle chain, not the top of its group, so per the standing 'never substitute a subsidiary LEI for a parent' discipline it was excluded rather than registered under either the Cognita Holdings subsidiary or the unrecognizable Lernen Topco/Bidco SPV names. 4/10 landed, 6 more needed to reach the 10-slot bar.\", :companies [#:company{:legal-name \"Bright Horizons Family Solutions Inc.\", :lei \"2549009BKSVTM7UEYT38\", :lei-source-url \"https://api.gleif.org/api/v1/lei-records?filter[entity.legalName]=Bright Horizons Family Solutions\", :repo \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-2549009bksvtm7ueyt38\", :status :done, :tos-doc-count 1, :tos-source-url \"https://www.brighthorizons.com/about/terms/about/terms-use\"} #:company{:legal-name \"Nord Anglia Education, Inc.\", :lei \"549300KPBTIINY0VBM50\", :lei-source-url \"https://api.gleif.org/api/v1/lei-records/549300KPBTIINY0VBM50\", :repo \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-549300kpbtiiny0vbm50\", :status :done, :tos-doc-count 1, :tos-source-url \"https://www.nordangliaeducation.com/legal-notice\"} #:company{:legal-name \"Childbase Partnership Limited\", :lei \"213800WJ8ELJ2XWXAG57\", :lei-source-url \"https://api.gleif.org/api/v1/lei-records/213800WJ8ELJ2XWXAG57\", :repo \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-213800wj8elj2xwxag57\", :status :done, :tos-doc-count 1, :tos-source-url \"https://childbasepartnership.com/terms-and-conditions/\"} #:company{:legal-name \"G8 Education Limited\", :lei \"5299008FNTQ0LDQ3UZ44\", :lei-source-url \"https://api.gleif.org/api/v1/lei-records/5299008FNTQ0LDQ3UZ44\", :repo \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-lei-5299008fntq0ldq3uz44\", :status :done, :tos-doc-count 1, :tos-source-url \"https://g8